  "articleBody": "It's super frustrating when you look at your baseboards and they just don't seem right. Maybe there are visible gaps, the corners are separating, or they're just not sitting flush against the wall. This can happen for a few reasons, and knowing what to look for can help you decide on the next steps. One common issue is that the boards weren't properly acclimated to the room before installation, causing them to warp or shrink. Another big one is inaccurate measurements or cuts, leading to pieces that are either too short or ill-fitting at the corners. Also, if the baseboards weren't securely fastened into the wall studs, they can pull away over time, especially with normal house movement. Uneven floors or walls are also a frequent culprit, making it tough to get a seamless look. You might try some minor caulking for very small gaps, but if the issues are more significant, you're likely looking at a re-do. If you’re seeing significant gaps, separating joints, or if the baseboards are actively pulling away from the wall, it’s a clear sign that a professional's touch is needed. These aren't just aesthetic issues; improperly installed baseboards can be less durable. Don't stress out; HH Remodeling LLC has the expertise to diagnose these problems and get your baseboards looking perfect and staying put.",
  "datePublished": "2026-08-09"
